=== SUMMARY ===
T1 interrupted keys: 48,411 models (ct-triggered restart/advance/pause on 351 trigger sets, pt-triggered, phase slip,
   word restart x 24 segmentations, line restart; L = 1..26 and non-repeating) -> 11,077 distinct with >= 8 checks,
   over 842,054 alphabets x 5 Quagmire arrangements x vig/beau + Quag IV over 116^2 clue pairs.
   K4: 0 hits (chance ~0.03); shuffled: 0, 0. Clue-only at >= 6 checks: K4 0 (shuffled 0 x5).
   Alphabet-free version (arbitrary alphabet per key position): K4 inside the shuffled range for every family (uninformative);
   single low-p fit line_restart L=7 (p=0.013 per model, ~0.3 after the 25 L values; rests on R->P at 27 and 65).
T2 Wheatstone 27/26: 21,893,404 structured outer rings, arbitrary inner alphabet: K4 0 pass (shuffled 0,0,0).
T3 base-27 groups: 22,735,458 embeddings x {Z27, Z3^3, Z9xZ3 (2 splits)}: periodic L=1..20,22,23 (>= 7 checks), ct-autokey and
   pt-autokey lags 1..26: K4 0 hits (chance ~0.05); shuffled 0, 0.
Side check: ANY periodic cipher with independent per-class alphabets is impossible for L = 1-7, 9, 10, 14, 15, 17, 21, 25
   (positions 24/66 both C=V with P=T/L, and 31/73 both C=K with P=A/K: any scheme that reuses one substitution at
   distance 42 is excluded, i.e. every period dividing 42).
Bonus affine/sign-mix: periodic affine L=1..10 and per-class Vig/Beau mixing L=1..10: 0 hits (L>=11 undecidable,
   K4 = chance).
No candidate decryption; nothing approaches a solve.
